Q: Is there a way to make escaping characters work in Vue.js in this case? A: <p><code>v-html</code> will not add escape characters.  Your text input must have already been escaped; The source that provides the property has already escaped the text before it is sent in as a property.</p>
<p>You need to fix that before the value is sent in, or by unescaping in your consuming component by adding a computed property, or creating a filter.</p>
<p>See this pen.  <a href="https://codepen.io/Flamenco/pen/xovKLq" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://codepen.io/Flamenco/pen/xovKLq</a></p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>        &lt;div v-html='message'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div v-html='message2'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div v-html='message3'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div v-html='computed3'&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

    data: () =&gt; ({
        message: &quot;Hello \&quot;World\&quot;&quot;,
        message2: `Hello \&quot;World\&quot;`,
        message3: 'Hello \\&quot;World\\&quot;', // this one is your property.
      }),

    computed: { 
     computed3() {
          return this.message3.replace(/\\&quot;/g, '&quot;');
        }
    }
</code></pre>
<p>I recommend dealing with this by fixing the source though...</p>

