Q: How to detect which item is in focus in HorizontalMultiBrowseCarousel from Material3 in Jetpack Compose? A: <p>You can actually use <code>currentItem</code> from <code>rememberCarouselState()</code> to determine which item is currently focused.</p>
<pre><code>val carouselState = rememberCarouselState { someItems.count() }

HorizontalMultiBrowseCarousel(
    state = carouselState,
    // ...
) { i -&gt;
    val someItem = someItems[i]

    val isFocused = carouselState.currentItem == i

    // your content here
}
</code></pre>
<p>This way, isFocused will be true only for the currently focused (enlarged) item, and you can use it to show/hide text or apply any UI changes.</p>
